## § {{N}} · {{owner file or gap}} — {{what it produces}} ({{n}} issues, {{new | recurring — was § M of sonar-NNN-1}})

| Rule | Quality · severity | Location in project | Message |
|---|---|---|---|
| `{{java:Sxxxx}}` | {{MAINTAINABILITY · MEDIUM}} | `{{path}}:{{line}}` | {{message}} |

**What happened.** {{The construct, how many times, main vs test. Quote the rule's
`root_cause` in one sentence when it explains the risk better than the message.}}

**Recurring.** {{Only for a recurring group whose previous file already proposed the fix at
the owner: say where that fix stands — not merged upstream, or merged and not pulled here
with `/arch-adopt`. Omit otherwise.}}

**Why.** {{The owner, by path and line inside `.claude/`, and how the construct reaches the
project from there: copied verbatim, prescribed by the norm, missing from Checkstyle, or
not covered by anything. If `doctor` reports the owner as edited since the export, say so —
the meta-repository's version may not carry the defect.}}

**Fix at the owner.** {{The file in `.claude/`, the change, and the enforcement that keeps it
from coming back: a Checkstyle check, an ArchUnit rule, a line in the norm. Concrete — a
path and the shape of the change.}}

**Fix here.** {{Optional: what to change in this project now, through `/new-feature` or by
hand. Omit when the fix at the owner is enough.}}

Rejected alternative: {{muting the rule, `sonar.issue.ignore`, `// NOSONAR` — and why it hides
the signal instead of removing the cause. Omit when nobody would propose one.}}

